{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JRLNQo6p4goHwshLN54KLz","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"Created schemas/Coding Session.md\\ntitle: Coding Session\\npermalink: ms/schemas/coding-session\\nchecksum: 1ee599269a36d18390991235f17e864b25a710842bec5e9ba2be8c5134fb3041\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb4d9816-3409-4eaf-94e5-b5f11754b047","uuid":"678b6927-cf9c-41bf-9e3d-96f6ec910136","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:42:11.533Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"Created schemas/Coding Session.md\\ntitle: Coding Session\\npermalink: ms/schemas/coding-session\\nchecksum: 1ee599269a36d18390991235f17e864b25a710842bec5e9ba2be8c5134fb3041\"}","_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"Basic Memory","version":"4.1.3"},"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}},"structuredContent":{"result":"Created schemas/Coding Session.md\ntitle: Coding Session\npermalink: ms/schemas/coding-session\nchecksum: 1ee599269a36d18390991235f17e864b25a710842bec5e9ba2be8c5134fb3041"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JRLNQo6p4goHwshLN54KLz","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf9MdzheUHjaWU4nkXVJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AgHfyru1cTNxWntAYhupHX","name":"mcp__basic-memory__bm_write","input":{"project":"ms","directory":"schemas","note_type":"schema","title":"Decision","content":"# Decision\n\nA **DecisionNote** is a durable record of a real choice — one with alternatives\nand a rationale, not a passing preference. Basic Memory host integrations\nencourage agents to capture these as decisions are made or explicitly requested.\n\nDecisions are found by structured recall:\n`bm_search(filters={\"type\": \"decision\", \"status\": \"open\"})`.\n\n## What makes a good DecisionNote\n\n- **decision** — state the choice plainly.\n- **rationale** + **alternative** — why this, and what was rejected. This is the\n  part that saves a future session from relitigating the same ground.\n- **consequence** — what the choice commits the work to.\n- **affects** / **supersedes** — relations that wire the decision into the graph.\n\n## Frontmatter\n\n`type: decision` plus `status` make decisions queryable. Capture decisions\nsparingly — one note per genuine decision, not per opinion. Validation is `warn`,\nnever blocking.","metadata":{"entity":"Decision","version":1,"schema":{"decision":"string, the choice that was made","rationale?":"string, why this choice over the alternatives","alternative?(array)":"string, options that were considered and not taken","consequence?(array)":"string, what this decision commits us to","context?":"string, the situation that prompted the decision","affects?(array)":"Entity, work or notes this decision bears on","supersedes?":"Entity, a prior decision this one replaces"},"settings":{"validation":"warn","frontmatter":{"status?(enum, lifecycle of the decision)":["open","accepted","superseded","rejected"],"decided?":"string, when the decision was made (ISO timestamp)","project?":"string, the Basic Memory project this decision belongs to"}}}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3111,"cache_read_input_tokens":30553,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3111},"output_tokens":49,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb4d9816-3409-4eaf-94e5-b5f11754b047","uuid":"849bbc2c-ff4c-4145-b24d-79fe45adda3b","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:42:13.342Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf9Mdn4XXFsTEN8hT3Er","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AgHfyru1cTNxWntAYhupHX","display_name":"Write note","server_display_name":"Basic Memory","tool_name":"bm_write"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AgHfyru1cTNxWntAYhupHX","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"Created schemas/Decision.md\\ntitle: Decision\\npermalink: ms/schemas/decision\\nchecksum: a205c5f88539669d6e00aff64cc33e14c14accfae825fdaaaf01d6e60e590307\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb4d9816-3409-4eaf-94e5-b5f11754b047","uuid":"bb2cf395-fd54-4bd4-a275-aa2f6a6fc29a","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:42:13.612Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"Created schemas/Decision.md\\ntitle: Decision\\npermalink: ms/schemas/decision\\nchecksum: a205c5f88539669d6e00aff64cc33e14c14accfae825fdaaaf01d6e60e590307\"}","_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"Basic Memory","version":"4.1.3"},"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}},"structuredContent":{"result":"Created schemas/Decision.md\ntitle: Decision\npermalink: ms/schemas/decision\nchecksum: a205c5f88539669d6e00aff64cc33e14c14accfae825fdaaaf01d6e60e590307"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AgHfyru1cTNxWntAYhupHX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf9MdzheUHjaWU4nkXVJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011a7cAkncbrEww9RMFmaD6F","name":"mcp__basic-memory__bm_write","input":{"project":"ms","directory":"schemas","note_type":"schema","title":"Task","content":"# Task\n\nA **Task** is work-in-progress tracked as a note, so it survives context\ncompaction and shows up in the next session's brief. This schema is the same one\nthe framework-agnostic `memory-tasks` skill defines — kept identical here so the\nplugin and the skill agree on the shape. For the full task workflow (creating,\nupdating, completing), use that skill.\n\nTasks are found by the SessionStart hook via structured recall:\n`bm_search(filters={\"type\": \"task\", \"status\": \"active\"})`.\n\n## Frontmatter vs observations\n\nPut queryable fields (`status`, `priority`, `current_step`) in frontmatter so\n`filters` can find them, and mirror them as `- [status] active`\nobservations so `bm_schema(command=\"validate\")` sees them. `note_type=\"Task\"` is stored as\nlowercase `task` in frontmatter, so search with `note_types=[\"task\"]`.\nValidation is `warn` — advisory, never blocking.","metadata":{"entity":"Task","version":1,"schema":{"description":"string, what needs to be done","status?(enum, current state)":["active","blocked","done","abandoned"],"assigned_to?":"string, who is working on this","steps?(array)":"string, ordered steps to complete","current_step?":"integer, which step number we're on (1-indexed)","context?":"string, key context needed to resume after memory loss","started?":"string, when work began","completed?":"string, when work finished","blockers?(array)":"string, what's preventing progress","parent_task?":"Task, parent task if this is a subtask"},"settings":{"validation":"warn"}}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3111,"cache_read_input_tokens":30553,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3111},"output_tokens":49,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb4d9816-3409-4eaf-94e5-b5f11754b047","uuid":"f27e1ddc-455a-467d-b2eb-42951e76069e","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:42:15.792Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf9Mdn4XXFsTEN8hT3Er","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011a7cAkncbrEww9RMFmaD6F","display_name":"Write note","server_display_name":"Basic Memory","tool_name":"bm_write"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011a7cAkncbrEww9RMFmaD6F","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"Created schemas/Task.md\\ntitle: Task\\npermalink: ms/schemas/task\\nchecksum: 3592ddf959a477a8ce0afeaec0ca2a93255203407bbd9189ca3db4c99e1d6531\\n\\n## Similar existing notes\\nThis note looks similar to notes that already exist. Did you mean to write to one of these?\\n- Coding Session (`schemas/Coding Session.md`)\\n- Decision (`schemas/Decision.md`)\\n\\n| If it is... | Then |\\n|---|---|\\n| The same topic | `bm_edit(identifier='schemas/Coding Session.md', command='append', content='...', project='ms')`, then `bm_delete(identifier='schemas/Task.md', project='ms')` |\\n| Related but distinct | Add a relation here, e.g. `- relates_to [[Coding Session]]` |\\n| Unrelated | Nothing to do |\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb4d9816-3409-4eaf-94e5-b5f11754b047","uuid":"ab736b9a-caa2-4304-b372-d5bb15851938","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:42:16.047Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"Created schemas/Task.md\\ntitle: Task\\npermalink: ms/schemas/task\\nchecksum: 3592ddf959a477a8ce0afeaec0ca2a93255203407bbd9189ca3db4c99e1d6531\\n\\n## Similar existing notes\\nThis note looks similar to notes that already exist. Did you mean to write to one of these?\\n- Coding Session (`schemas/Coding Session.md`)\\n- Decision (`schemas/Decision.md`)\\n\\n| If it is... | Then |\\n|---|---|\\n| The same topic | `bm_edit(identifier='schemas/Coding Session.md', command='append', content='...', project='ms')`, then `bm_delete(identifier='schemas/Task.md', project='ms')` |\\n| Related but distinct | Add a relation here, e.g. `- relates_to [[Coding Session]]` |\\n| Unrelated | Nothing to do |\"}","_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"Basic Memory","version":"4.1.3"},"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}},"structuredContent":{"result":"Created schemas/Task.md\ntitle: Task\npermalink: ms/schemas/task\nchecksum: 3592ddf959a477a8ce0afeaec0ca2a93255203407bbd9189ca3db4c99e1d6531\n\n## Similar existing notes\nThis note looks similar to notes that already exist. Did you mean to write to one of these?\n- Coding Session (`schemas/Coding Session.md`)\n- Decision (`schemas/Decision.md`)\n\n| If it is... | Then |\n|---|---|\n| The same topic | `bm_edit(identifier='schemas/Coding Session.md', command='append', content='...', project='ms')`, then `bm_delete(identifier='schemas/Task.md', project='ms')` |\n| Related but distinct | Add a relation here, e.g. `- relates_to [[Coding Session]]` |\n| Unrelated | Nothing to do |"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011a7cAkncbrEww9RMFmaD6F","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
