{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GJWHbnQQJfeDLsCTkS6KSD","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"title\":\"Coding Session\",\"permalink\":\"ms/schemas/coding-session\",\"file_path\":\"schemas/Coding Session.md\",\"content\":\"\\n# Coding Session\\n\\nA **CodingSession** is a resumable engineering checkpoint whose repository\\nidentity is structured and queryable. Required Git fields make it possible to\\nfind the exact work cursor without parsing prose.\\n\\nExamples:\\n\\n`bm_search(note_types=[\\\"coding_session\\\"], filters={\\\"repository\\\": \\\"owner/repo\\\"})`\\n\\n`bm_search(note_types=[\\\"coding_session\\\"], filters={\\\"pull_request_number\\\": \\\"123\\\"})`\\n\\n`bm_search(note_types=[\\\"coding_session\\\"], filters={\\\"agent\\\": \\\"codex\\\", \\\"session_id\\\": \\\"<id>\\\"})`\\n\\nPull-request fields are optional because valid coding work can precede a pull\\nrequest. When a pull request exists, checkpoint writers populate the complete\\npull-request field set. Multiple checkpoints from one agent chat share the\\n`agent` and `session_id` pair; session IDs alone are not cross-agent identity.\\nEach new checkpoint can link to its verified predecessor with\\n`continues [[Previous checkpoint title]]`. New writers use the shared fields.\\nLegacy agent-specific session fields remain accepted for existing notes; do not\\nrewrite old checkpoints or infer missing session IDs.\",\"frontmatter\":null,\"checksum\":\"1ee599269a36d18390991235f17e864b25a710842bec5e9ba2be8c5134fb3041\",\"section\":null,\"start_line\":56,\"end_line\":78,\"total_lines\":78,\"has_more\":false,\"next_start_line\":null,\"next_end_line\":null}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb4d9816-3409-4eaf-94e5-b5f11754b047","uuid":"4cc31481-02ef-495a-a183-9737821bad09","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:42:18.838Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"title\":\"Coding Session\",\"permalink\":\"ms/schemas/coding-session\",\"file_path\":\"schemas/Coding Session.md\",\"content\":\"\\n# Coding Session\\n\\nA **CodingSession** is a resumable engineering checkpoint whose repository\\nidentity is structured and queryable. Required Git fields make it possible to\\nfind the exact work cursor without parsing prose.\\n\\nExamples:\\n\\n`bm_search(note_types=[\\\"coding_session\\\"], filters={\\\"repository\\\": \\\"owner/repo\\\"})`\\n\\n`bm_search(note_types=[\\\"coding_session\\\"], filters={\\\"pull_request_number\\\": \\\"123\\\"})`\\n\\n`bm_search(note_types=[\\\"coding_session\\\"], filters={\\\"agent\\\": \\\"codex\\\", \\\"session_id\\\": \\\"<id>\\\"})`\\n\\nPull-request fields are optional because valid coding work can precede a pull\\nrequest. When a pull request exists, checkpoint writers populate the complete\\npull-request field set. Multiple checkpoints from one agent chat share the\\n`agent` and `session_id` pair; session IDs alone are not cross-agent identity.\\nEach new checkpoint can link to its verified predecessor with\\n`continues [[Previous checkpoint title]]`. New writers use the shared fields.\\nLegacy agent-specific session fields remain accepted for existing notes; do not\\nrewrite old checkpoints or infer missing session IDs.\",\"frontmatter\":null,\"checksum\":\"1ee599269a36d18390991235f17e864b25a710842bec5e9ba2be8c5134fb3041\",\"section\":null,\"start_line\":56,\"end_line\":78,\"total_lines\":78,\"has_more\":false,\"next_start_line\":null,\"next_end_line\":null}","_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"Basic Memory","version":"4.1.3"}},"structuredContent":{"title":"Coding Session","permalink":"ms/schemas/coding-session","file_path":"schemas/Coding Session.md","content":"\n# Coding Session\n\nA **CodingSession** is a resumable engineering checkpoint whose repository\nidentity is structured and queryable. Required Git fields make it possible to\nfind the exact work cursor without parsing prose.\n\nExamples:\n\n`bm_search(note_types=[\"coding_session\"], filters={\"repository\": \"owner/repo\"})`\n\n`bm_search(note_types=[\"coding_session\"], filters={\"pull_request_number\": \"123\"})`\n\n`bm_search(note_types=[\"coding_session\"], filters={\"agent\": \"codex\", \"session_id\": \"<id>\"})`\n\nPull-request fields are optional because valid coding work can precede a pull\nrequest. When a pull request exists, checkpoint writers populate the complete\npull-request field set. Multiple checkpoints from one agent chat share the\n`agent` and `session_id` pair; session IDs alone are not cross-agent identity.\nEach new checkpoint can link to its verified predecessor with\n`continues [[Previous checkpoint title]]`. New writers use the shared fields.\nLegacy agent-specific session fields remain accepted for existing notes; do not\nrewrite old checkpoints or infer missing session IDs.","frontmatter":null,"checksum":"1ee599269a36d18390991235f17e864b25a710842bec5e9ba2be8c5134fb3041","section":null,"start_line":56,"end_line":78,"total_lines":78,"has_more":false,"next_start_line":null,"next_end_line":null}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GJWHbnQQJfeDLsCTkS6KSD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf9NfaEK15yKucCvGnDx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LQWqKv4iVadx3Nz9o5WXbg","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/ep-7_dv_z0f/work/ms; mkdir -p .claude; f=.claude/settings.local.json; [ -f $f ] && cat $f; cat > $f <<'EOF'\n{\"basicMemory\":{\"primaryProject\":\"ms\",\"secondaryProjects\":[],\"captureFolder\":\"sessions\",\"rememberFolder\":\"bm-remember\",\"recallTimeframe\":\"3d\",\"preCompactCapture\":\"extractive\",\"sessionProfile\":\"coding\",\"repository\":\"ms\",\"captureEvents\":true,\"placementConventions\":\"Starting point, not a scaffold; structure stays emergent.\\n- decisions/ for engineering decisions (type: decision)\\n- tasks/ for work in progress (type: task)\\n- sessions/ for coding checkpoints\\n- notes/ for research and general knowledge\\n- schemas/ holds note schemas\",\"teamProjects\":{}},\"outputStyle\":\"basic-memory\"}\nEOF\npython3 -m json.tool $f >/dev/null && echo valid; git status --short; git check-ignore .claude/settings.local.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3499,"cache_read_input_tokens":33664,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3499},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb4d9816-3409-4eaf-94e5-b5f11754b047","uuid":"d2d1094c-880f-44dc-bc57-0ac3fd83038c","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:42:21.169Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf9NfLbxC5bb4VAtnNPE"}
