{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf9Qd2zRJmdeaneZm3Yr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Basic Memory is set up for this repo. The proactive-capture style needs a session restart to take effect.\n\n- **Project:** I created a new project, `ms`, at `~/basic-memory-ms`. The default path `~/basic-memory/ms` was rejected because it sits inside the existing `main` project, so I used a sibling folder.\n- **Session profile:** coding, with `repository: \"ms\"`. There is no git remote, so I used the directory name as you said.\n- **Schemas:** I seeded Coding Session, Decision and Task, since the project was empty. I checked the Coding Session file on disk, and its `schema` and `settings` are nested objects, not strings.\n- **Placement:** this is a suggested starting structure, not learned from existing notes, because the project is empty. It uses `decisions/`, `tasks/`, `sessions/` and `notes/`, and no folders are created until notes land in them.\n- **Settings:** I merged them into `.claude/settings.local.json`, which is personal and not committed. The file is currently untracked and not gitignored, so it could get committed by accident. Lifecycle-event capture is on, and the `basic-memory` output style is on.\n- **Shared skills:** I installed the `memory-*` skills globally with `npx skills add basicmachines-co/basic-memory/skills -g`. This repo isn't the skills' source repo, so nothing was overwritten.\n- **Smoke test:**\n  - The open-decision query ran cleanly with 0 results.\n  - The schema search returned all three schemas.\n  - `bm hook status` found the settings, with primary project `ms`, coding profile, repository `ms` and capture on.\n  - The hook inbox has 3 pending envelopes, 0 archived, and has never been flushed.\n  - `bm hook status` reports \"checkpoint on compact: off\", although the settings say `preCompactCapture: \"extractive\"`. I didn't investigate it.\n\nRecall and the PreCompact checkpoint work now. The proactive-capture reflexes only start in a new Claude Code session.\n\nDone — I'll use this from the next message. Run `/basic-memory:bm-status` anytime to see what I'm tracking."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":483,"cache_read_input_tokens":39742,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":483},"output_tokens":715,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb4d9816-3409-4eaf-94e5-b5f11754b047","uuid":"71b6db9b-4578-4c6a-bf80-06cc3bd2f9f1","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:42:47.935Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf9QcqLyfJy9iELaqwUE"}
